{"id":"CQ-001","category":"code_quality","criterion":"error_handling","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/guard-yield.sh","line":470,"code_snippet":"if source \"$HEREDOC_LIB\" 2>/dev/null && declare -F heredoc_nonexec >/dev/null; then","finding":"Optional heredoc classifier is sourced in the main shell; the library sources the fence with BDB_LIB_ONLY=1, which the PR's fence does not honour, so the fence runs as a hook on empty stdin and exit 0s the generator before any output is written.","reasoning_trace":"Read guard-yield.sh 465-483; grep BDB_LIB_ONLY in head fence (none) vs base fence (line 771); read heredoc-classifier.sh:19; reproduced with bash -c 'source <head fence> </dev/null; echo REACHED' (no output, rc 0) vs base fence (REACHED).","critique":"Never source optional code in the shell that owns the outputs.","remediation":"Probe in a subshell: ( source \"$HEREDOC_LIB\" && declare -F heredoc_nonexec ) >/dev/null 2>&1 || die 3; or classify in a subshell. Add the BDB_LIB_ONLY guard to this PR's fence.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html"]}
{"id":"SEC-001","category":"security","criterion":"logging_integrity","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/scripts/guard-yield.sh","line":443,"code_snippet":"for f in \"$AUDIT_LOG\" \"$AUDIT_LOG\".*; do","finding":"The yield reads rotated segments audit.jsonl.* that no writer creates; mutation-logger truncates in place to the last 1000 rows at 10 MB, so post-truncation counts silently undercount while window_days stays 30; the glob also catches the transient audit.jsonl.tmp.","reasoning_trace":"Read guard-yield.sh 26-27, 441-455, 551-553; grep mutation-logger.sh 187-194 (tail -n 1000 > .tmp && mv); grep for other audit.jsonl writers (none rotate); GY-2 fabricates audit.jsonl.1.","critique":"A reporting tool must surface when its input window is shorter than it claims.","remediation":"Match \"$AUDIT_LOG\".[0-9]* only; emit truncated:true / window_effective_from when the earliest row ts lies inside the window; or rotate into audit.jsonl.1 in mutation-logger.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/223.html","https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/778.html"]}
{"id":"ARCH-001","category":"architecture","criterion":"change_discipline","severity":"MEDIUM","score":3,"file":"head/.claude/skills/implementing-tasks/SKILL.md","line":28,"code_snippet":"    permission: read-write","finding":"App-zone permission widened from read to read-write in an unrelated PR with no DEC row and no mention in the description; CLAUDE.loa.md and the GLOSSARY still say confirm-writes.","reasoning_trace":"Diff hunk; grep .claude/scripts and .claude/hooks for zones readers (zone-write-guard reads grimoires/loa/zones.yaml, review-scope reads .loa-version.json) so effect is prose-only; dissent DISS-C-003 in both rounds.","critique":"Policy changes travel alone or with a decision record.","remediation":"Add a DEC row and one sentence to the PR description, or split the hunk out.","confidence":"high","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1059.html"]}
