{"id":"CQ-003","category":"code_quality","criterion":"concurrency","severity":"LOW","score":4,"file":"head/evals/harness/run-arms.sh","line":287,"code_snippet":"until mkdir \"$lockd\" 2>/dev/null; do n=$((n + 1)); [[ $n -gt 50 ]] && return 0; sleep 0.1; done","finding":"Suite-status lock wait returns success after ~5 s without aggregating; cleanup never removes the status lock, so an interrupted run leaves it behind.","reasoning_trace":"Read run-arms.sh 244-248, 285-304.","remediation":"Log the abandoned wait; remove the lock in cleanup; or write via per-pid temp + mv.","confidence":"medium","references":["https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/667.html"]}
